NV_PK(12,{"belonging to the people who lived in a place first before others arrived":"","some say the fish got its name from an indigenous language":"","record":"","something written down so people can know about it later":"","a record from 1717 lists milkfish in the ponds":"","a long running beef hot pot restaurant in yongkang tainan the broth simmers for hours from beef bones and vegetables and the beef is fresh never frozen from that day's local cattle stir fried beef offal intestine and heart are local favourites it is often full in winter and a popular place for family dinners":"","a story stop the century old birthplace of danzai noodles where the cook still sits on a low stool at a charcoal stove":"","a story stop a tainan breakfast milkfish congee with a fried dough stick opens very early and closes when it sells out":"","a story stop coffin bread is said to have been born in this market once called sakariba":"","a story stop anping's best known shrimp rolls fried to order":"","a story stop an old shop near chihkan tower silky bowl rice cake with fish soup is a classic tainan brunch":""});